# Laptop Exec - SSH-First

`~/mounts/` is optional SSHFS (may be STALE). Truth = laptop via `laptop-exec`. Do not ask to enable SSHFS.

## No trial-and-error

Hooks deny on `/mounts/`: Read, Write, Edit, EditNotebook, StrReplace, Delete, Grep, Glob, and heavy Shell. Deny is **expected**. **Do not retry.** First I/O = Shell + `laptop-exec` (or windows-mcp per hybrid below). Project `hooks.json` must stay `{"version":1,"hooks":{}}`.

| Denied | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Read | `laptop-exec read -p ID REL` (or windows-mcp `FileSystem` on Windows when ready) |
| Write/Edit/StrReplace | `laptop-exec write -p ID REL` (full stdin) / MCP `FileSystem` write |
| Grep/Glob | `laptop-exec rg -p ID PATTERN [pathspec]` (**not** MCP — content search) |
| heavy Shell | `laptop-exec git\|run\|rg\|read -p ID …` / MCP `PowerShell` when ready |

**rg is NOT ripgrep:** never `-i`/`-l`/`-n`/`--glob` (rejected; old hangs). Pathspecs only.

**Task spawn is ALWAYS allowed.** Every Task `prompt` MUST paste the SSH-first block from the `laptop-exec` skill (`-p ID`; no Read/Grep on mounts; no `rg -i/--glob`; hybrid note). Prefer ≤4 parallel `laptop-exec` (hard cap 8). On deny, run `NEXT:`.

Both flag orders: `laptop-exec -p ID read REL` and `laptop-exec read -p ID REL`.

## Hybrid (Windows only)

- **Keep laptop-exec** always (Mac, `git`, content `rg`, MCP down).
- When Cursor MCP `windows-mcp` is ready: prefer it for FileSystem/UI/Screenshot/PowerShell.
- Never delete or skip laptop-exec because MCP exists.
- Full routing: skill `laptop-exec` (+ `reference-windows-mcp.md`).

## Paths / boot

- Repo-relative only for laptop-exec — never `/home/$USER/mounts/ID/...`
- windows-mcp paths: absolute Windows under project root (not Desktop-relative)
- Windows `read` may mojibake non-ASCII; `write` is binary-safe
- `laptop-exec status` → DOWN => user `connect.bat/sh`; STALE mount + UP tunnel => still laptop-exec
- Resolve: `-p` > workspace env/`PWD` under mounts > `ACTIVE_MOUNT`

## Allowed without laptop-exec

`/tmp/**`, `~/.cursor/**`, non-mount paths; light shell (`echo`, `ls`, `python3`); any command containing `laptop-exec`; Cursor MCP `windows-mcp` tools when that server is ready.

## Mux / sudo

8 session slots; shared ControlMaster; do not stress-test the tunnel. Sudo: `sudo-from-laptop --smart|--sepidz -- …` — never ask for a password.
